 "known_limitations": [
  "The full VCD traces stay local (2 MB to 38 MB each, .vcd is not whitelisted); only their sha256, the small derived tables and the sample rows are committed, so a reviewer must re-run the chain to see waveforms.",
  "R4 re-published the evidence from the frozen R2 run r2_20261021; no new simulation was started. A reviewer who wants fresh waveforms must re-run --run-rtl, and the export refuses a cached run whose RTL/TB/checker/reader digests differ. The two entry cases that call do_export() stub the artefact builder and are labelled BOUNDARY_DIAGNOSTIC: they cover the recovery gate only, never a build or an export PASS.",
  "The cleanup repairs are exercised against injected faults in private fixtures. A real disk that refuses deletion (a full volume, a locked handle) is not reproduced here, and the guarantee stays: the transaction record survives an unfinished cleanup, so nothing is lost rather than recovered.",
  "The publish/recover guarantees stay what the tool can actually deliver: a caught-failure rollback plus a marker a later process can use. Multi-file power-loss atomicity is not claimed, and the two BOUNDARY_DIAGNOSTIC cases that call do_export() stub the artefact builder, so they cover the entry gate only, never a build.",
  "The numeric gates protect the delivered tables from a wrong value; they do not make the measurement itself more accurate, and no threshold, tolerance or endpoint was changed.",
  "pam_sel is a code. In Pure mode 7 is a symbol, not 15 uA; the eight current levels, trimming and the reference relationship remain NOT_RUN.",
  "Optical effective grey bits, LED I-V, array RC, final VLED/VSCAN and SOA are NOT_VERIFIED; an RTL pass proves none of them.",
  "One pre-existing unreachable large blob <blob:955497fb18ac> (3,583,407 bytes, dated 2026-10-14, not created by this round) makes the --mode objects scan FAIL. It is left exactly as found: no GC, no content printed, no gate relaxed, no history rewritten.",
  "This validator and this JSON prove field structure only. They do not verify remote truth, circuit behaviour, or that any recorded number is physically correct."
